---
args:
  - '--debug'
  - '--enable-usages'
  - '--enable-operations'
  # Without it, upgrading a dependency that is installed under its own short
  # name (function-auto-ready, provider-opentofu, …, as the crossplane-config
  # and crossplane-providers helmfiles do) puts that package into the Lock
  # twice: the dependency manager sees it missing during the revision swap and
  # installs a second copy under the derived name
  # (crossplane-contrib-function-auto-ready). After that no package resolves
  # ("node … already exists") until the copy is deleted by hand. Seen on
  # u26-kind3 for provider-opentofu and three functions; reproduced on a
  # throwaway kind cluster (Crossplane 2.3.3) for functions and providers,
  # and gone with this flag, also when it is turned on for an existing cluster.
  # Alpha. Side effect: when a Configuration is updated and needs a HIGHER
  # version of a dependency, Crossplane now upgrades the installed dependency
  # in place instead of failing. The short names have to stay: every
  # Composition calls its functions by name (functionRef.name).
  - '--enable-dependency-version-upgrades'

{{- if .Values.providers }}
provider:
  packages:
    {{- range .Values.providers }}
    - {{ . }}
    {{- end }}
{{- end }}
